>I'm a newbie to nethack and chrhack.  I recently ftp'ed both and i have 
>both up and running.  Walls and objects are really nice, but monsters are 
>only letters...Is that the way it's supposed to be or am I doing 

It's the CHRDATA.DAT file that counts. You need another one to show monsters
in a different way. I have sometimes seen alternate chrdata.dat's posted
here, the latest one was about two weeks ago..
Well, of course it is possible to edit the file yourself, there is a font
editor just for this purpose in the chrdata packet..

I guess basically the reason that the monsters are left as letters is so that
we old players wouldn't be too uncomfortable having to study another set of
sligtly different symbols for monsters instead of very easily distinguishable
(and already familiar) letters. It is easy to make the difference between a
'f' and a 'd', for example, but it is more difficult to draw good cat- and
dog-like characters in the limited amount of pixels so that you can see which
is which. And in some cases there are totally different looking creatures
that are printed with the same letter..
And maybe we even don't know HOW some monsters look like.. have you ever
seen a zruty, for example? Or a Jabberwock?

